<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Imsa to pay dividend.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Imsa to pay dividend.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders for Mexican steel and industrial company Grupo Imsa SA de CV on Tuesday agreed to a dividend of 0.04 pesos per share, the company said.</p>
<p>The cut-off date for holding coupons is April 24 with the dividend payable on April 29, Imsa said.  </p>
<p>&quot;The payment is the equivalent of 122.2 million pesos or approximately $15.5 million,&quot; Imsa said in a statement.</p>
<p>There are 2,771,700,000 shares in circulation.</p>
<p>Imsa, based in Monterrey, has interests in steel, automotive batteries and construction.</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez, Monterrey bureau, +528 345-7617))</p>
